# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provokes registered candidates in order, two at a time, including the bard target.
# bard/provo-picks owns the lastbeneficial input and the candidate list. Labels are the
# state: provoked and barding-break creatures wait, while the first two free candidates
# fight each other. A lone one waits, with no fallback onto an unregistered target.
# Q changes the bard target, not this order. No list remembers successful pairs.
#
# @ hotkeys Cancel Current Target
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   interval__provo_seen
#      How often the pool is looked over while pairs are being made, the same two
#      seconds bard/peace reads its labels on.
#
#   interval__provo_retry
#      How long the next round waits after one that found nothing to provoke, or could
#      not reach its pair. A new pick cuts it short. A plain failure needs no wait of its
#      own: "fail to incite anger" starts the 5 second peace/provo bar (cooldowns.xml).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! interval__provo_seen 2000
@setvar! interval__provo_retry 5000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ timer
#
#   timer__provo_seen, timer__provo_retry
#      Ready on the first pass.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
timer__provo_seen interval__provo_seen
timer__provo_retry interval__provo_retry


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__provo_first, var__provo_second
#      Scratch: the two enemies found free this round, provoked first onto second. 0 when
#      not found.
#
#   var__provo_dropped
#      Scratch: 1 when the round found an enemy dead or gone, so the pool is rebuilt.
#
#   var__provo_answer
#      Scratch: what the server answered, 0 nothing known, 1 provoked, 2 failed, 3 out of
#      reach, 4 the first one cannot be provoked, 5 the slot was not free yet.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! var__provo_first 0
@setvar! var__provo_second 0
@setvar! var__provo_dropped 0
@setvar! var__provo_answer 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ setup
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The candidate list is kept by bard/provo-picks. A refusal gets a new chance on Play.
if not listexists 'list__provo_keep'
    createlist 'list__provo_keep'
endif

removelist 'list__provo_never'
createlist 'list__provo_never'


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # PROVOKE
    #
    # Input is collected earlier by bard/provo-picks, including during manual control
    # and cooldowns. A new registration refreshes the scan clocks. Dead, friendly and
    # far candidates leave on the next round, with no label read for registration.
    #
    # Pairs follow registration order, including the current bard target. A, B, C, D, E
    # gives A onto B, C onto D, and E waiting. A pacified candidate can still be provoked
    # (Bard Necro 02.P). Peace leaves provoked creatures alone.
    #
    # Peace and Provocation share one server slot (Bard Necro part 2), so this goes
    # before bard/peace and bard/disco in the pass and takes the slot, and Music, whenever
    # a pair is free. Peace and Provocation both last 51 seconds here (Bard Necro 01.D),
    # and Ensemble counts either effect alongside Discordance (Bard Necro part 2).
    #
    # The first enemy is targeted, then the second, and each goes into var__target_hold
    # just before. The Provocation cursor is harmful (user check, 2026-10-20), so the
    # second one ends up in lastharmful, and a refused first target leaves it on the
    # first. No block takes either for a new pick. This protects the cached bard target,
    # not the native harmful slot used by manual hotkeys.
    # The Journal lines this reads are read off first, so a line left over from a cast
    # cannot pass for this answer. The answers are the lines other Outlands bard scripts
    # read, and "fail to incite anger" is the one cooldowns.xml and the profile key on.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if var__provo_added = 1
        settimer "timer__provo_seen" interval__provo_seen
        settimer "timer__provo_retry" interval__provo_retry
    endif

    if var__fighting = 1 and list 'list__provo_candidates' >= 2 and timer "timer__provo_seen" >= interval__provo_seen and timer "timer__provo_retry" >= interval__provo_retry and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0 and cooldown "music" = 0 and skill "Provocation" > 0 and not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1 and var__my_instrument != 0 and not targetexists and not casting
        settimer "timer__provo_seen" 0
        @setvar! var__provo_first 0
        @setvar! var__provo_second 0
        @setvar! var__provo_dropped 0
        clearlist 'list__provo_keep'

        foreach provo_mob in list__provo_candidates
            if find provo_mob ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__provo_mob
                if dead alias__provo_mob
                    @setvar! var__provo_dropped 1
                elseif noto alias__provo_mob = "hostile" or noto alias__provo_mob = "criminal" or noto alias__provo_mob = "enemy" or noto alias__provo_mob = "murderer"
                    pushlist 'list__provo_keep' provo_mob

                    if var__provo_second = 0
                        if not inlist 'list__provo_never' provo_mob
                            if find provo_mob ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__provo_near
                                @unsetvar! label__provo_mob
                                @setvar! label__provo_mob 0
                                getlabel alias__provo_near label__provo_mob

                                if label__provo_mob = 0
                                    # No label means no known free barding slot.
                                elseif "provoked" in label__provo_mob or "barding break" in label__provo_mob
                                    # Busy, or cannot take one now.
                                elseif var__provo_first = 0
                                    @setvar! var__provo_first provo_mob
                                else
                                    @setvar! var__provo_second provo_mob
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif
                else
                    @setvar! var__provo_dropped 1
                endif
            else
                @setvar! var__provo_dropped 1
            endif
        endfor

        if var__provo_dropped = 1
            clearlist 'list__provo_candidates'

            foreach provo_mob in list__provo_keep
                pushlist 'list__provo_candidates' provo_mob
            endfor
        endif

        if var__provo_second = 0
            # Nothing to provoke: look again in five seconds, or at the next pick.
            settimer "timer__provo_retry" 0
        elseif not warmode and not targetexists and not casting
            if insysmsg "play successfully, provoking"
                # Read off, with the three below, before this round's answer.
            endif

            if insysmsg "too far away"
                # Read off.
            endif

            if insysmsg "Target cannot be seen"
                # Read off.
            endif

            if insysmsg "You must wait a few moments"
                # Read off.
            endif

            if insysmsg "fail to incite anger"
                # Read off.
            endif

            if insysmsg "incite that"
                # Read off.
            endif

            if insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                # Read off before this request.
            endif

            useskill 'Provocation'
            waitfortarget wait__bard_target

            # Answered once, the way bard/peace does.
            if not warmode and targetexists and insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                target var__my_instrument
                waitfortarget wait__bard_target

                if insysmsg "That is not a musical instrument"
                    @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
                endif
            endif

            # Validate both serials again after the cursor wait. A manual cursor is
            # left untouched in warmode, even if it carries the old harmful flag.
            if targetexists "harmful" and not warmode
                # Preserve a completed Q selection before our own target overwrites it.
                if find lastharmful ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                    @setvar! var__fresh_serial alias__fresh_target

                    if 0x40000000 > var__fresh_serial and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target and var__target_hold != alias__fresh_target
                        if not dead alias__fresh_target
                            if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                if config__chatty = 1
                                    overhead "[ target, set ]" 1288 var__combat_target
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif
                endif

                if find var__provo_first ground -1 -1 config__target_range and find var__provo_second ground -1 -1 config__target_range
                    if not dead var__provo_first and not dead var__provo_second
                        @setvar! var__target_hold var__provo_first
                        target var__provo_first
                        waitfortarget wait__bard_target

                        if targetexists "harmful" and not warmode
                            if find lastharmful ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__fresh_target
                                @setvar! var__fresh_serial alias__fresh_target

                                if 0x40000000 > var__fresh_serial and var__combat_target != alias__fresh_target and var__target_hold != alias__fresh_target
                                    if not dead alias__fresh_target
                                        if noto alias__fresh_target = "hostile" or noto alias__fresh_target = "criminal" or noto alias__fresh_target = "enemy" or noto alias__fresh_target = "murderer"
                                            @setvar! var__combat_target alias__fresh_target
                                            settimer "timer__target_grace" 0

                                            if config__chatty = 1
                                                overhead "[ target, set ]" 1288 var__combat_target
                                            endif
                                        endif
                                    endif
                                endif
                            endif

                            if find var__provo_first ground -1 -1 config__target_range and find var__provo_second ground -1 -1 config__target_range
                                if not dead var__provo_first and not dead var__provo_second
                                    @setvar! var__target_hold var__provo_second
                                    target var__provo_second
                                    wait wait__short
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif
                endif
            endif

            if targetexists "harmful" and not warmode
                hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                wait wait__short
            endif

            # The answer comes within a second. Read on every round until it does, with
            # no break: this loop sits inside the main one.
            @setvar! var__provo_answer 0

            for 5
                if var__provo_answer = 0 and not warmode
                    if insysmsg "play successfully, provoking"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 1
                    elseif insysmsg "fail to incite anger"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 2
                    elseif insysmsg "too far away" or insysmsg "Target cannot be seen"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 3
                    elseif insysmsg "incite that"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 4
                    elseif insysmsg "You must wait a few moments"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 5
                    else
                        wait wait__short
                    endif
                endif
            endfor

            # Success is observed on the next label scan, not stored as a permanent pair.
            # Rotate a failed first candidate behind the others and back off. No stop.
            if not warmode
                if var__provo_answer = 4
                    pushlist 'list__provo_never' var__provo_first
                    overhead "[ provo, wrong ]" 1288 var__provo_first
                elseif var__provo_answer = 5
                    settimer "timer__provo_retry" 0
                elseif var__provo_answer = 0 or var__provo_answer = 2 or var__provo_answer = 3
                    clearlist 'list__provo_keep'

                    foreach provo_mob in list__provo_candidates
                        if provo_mob != var__provo_first
                            pushlist 'list__provo_keep' provo_mob
                        endif
                    endfor

                    clearlist 'list__provo_candidates'

                    foreach provo_mob in list__provo_keep
                        pushlist 'list__provo_candidates' provo_mob
                    endfor

                    pushlist 'list__provo_candidates' var__provo_first
                    if var__provo_answer != 2
                        settimer "timer__provo_retry" 0
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif
    endif
